Human trafficking is a crime in which someone forces or coerces another person to perform labor or engage in sex acts for money. The <a href="https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Individuals-and-Families/Victims/Human-Trafficking" >Attorney General's Human Trafficking Initiative</a> and the&nbsp;<a href="https://ocjs.ohio.gov/anti-human-trafficking" >Governor&rsquo;s Human Trafficking Task Force</a> are actively fighting this terrible crime and ensuring resources are available for victims.
View <a href="https://data.ohio.gov/wps/portal/gov/data/view/ohio-human-trafficking-task-force-summary?visualize=true" >current statistics about human trafficking in Ohio</a>.
If you or someone you know is being used for someone else's profit, call the <strong>Ohio Human Trafficking Hotline</strong> at <strong>1-844-363-6448. </strong>If you are in danger right now, dial 911.&nbsp;

The <a href="http://www.ohio.org/" >Ohio Tourism (Ohio.org) website</a> is your source of information about the amazing destinations and experiences you will find in Ohio.&nbsp;From outdoor adventures and amazing arts scenes to engaging events and family fun, Ohio is the heart of it all.&nbsp;
Explore things to do, find places to stay, learn about festivals and events, and get inspired for your next Ohio adventure.
Be sure to sign up for the Ohio Tourism newsletter and get your copy of the free Ohio Travel Guide.

Ohio's law enforcement agencies work together with the Attorney General's office to locate and recover <a href="https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/missingpersons" >missing children and adults</a>. You can view open missing persons cases on the Attorney General's website.&nbsp;
To report a missing person, contact your <a href="/wps/portal/gov/site/residents/resources/law-enforcement" >local law enforcement agency</a>.&nbsp;
Ohioans can be notified of active missing persons cases by signing up to receive <a href="https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Law-Enforcement/Local-Law-Enforcement/Ohio-Amber-Plan" >Amber Alerts (missing and endangered children)</a>, <a href="https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Law-Enforcement/Local-Law-Enforcement/Missing-Adult-Alert/Missing-Alert-Sign-Up?type=Missing%20Adult" >Missing Adult Alerts</a>, or <a href="https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Law-Enforcement/Local-Law-Enforcement/Blue-Alert?type=Blue" >Blue Alerts (injured or missing law enforcement officers)</a>.

The <a href="https://gateway.ohio.gov/" >Ohio Business&nbsp;Gateway</a>&nbsp;helps Ohioans access services and submit transactions and payments with many state agencies.
